  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The sudden resignation of Vice President Gibran has triggered a series of administrative and political responses within the Indonesian government. The People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) has initiated discussions to address the vacancy, focusing on the verification process for selecting a replacement. Amidst these developments, political figures and parties, including Gerindra, PSI, and PPP, have offered differing perspectives on the transition, ranging from commitments to maintain support for the existing administration to calls for political elites to remain focused on addressing citizens' primary concerns. Economic analysts and officials, such as Airlangga Hartarto, have emphasized the importance of legal certainty to maintain investor confidence and domestic economic stability. Furthermore, public discourse has extended to the logistical aspects of the resignation, including the specifications of retirement benefits, security protocols provided by Paspampres, and discussions regarding constitutional eligibility for future electoral participation.",
